.TH DROIDCAM-CLI 1 "November 2026" "droidcam 2.1.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
droidcam-cli \- use a phone running the DroidCam app as a webcam
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B droidcam-cli
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIip\fR \fIport\fR
.br
.B droidcam-cli
[\fIoptions\fR] adb \fIport\fR
.br
.B droidcam-cli
[\fIoptions\fR] ios \fIport\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connects to the DroidCam app on a phone (the app's default port is 4747), by Wi-Fi, by USB through adb or to an iPhone,
and writes the picture to a v4l2loopback virtual camera.
With several phones on adb, set ANDROID_SERIAL to the serial that "adb devices" lists.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Enable the sound.
.TP
.B \-v
Enable the video (the default).
.TP
.B \-vflip, \-hflip
Flip the picture vertically or horizontally.
.TP
.B \-nocontrols
Do not read the keyboard.
.TP
.BI \-dev= PATH
Use this v4l2loopback device instead of the first one found.
.TP
.BI \-size= WxH
The video size when the regular v4l2loopback module is used.
.SH AUTHORS
Dev47Apps.
